annot(#noCore)

#noCore
# The control for `dataArrow.ct`: the same chain with the sources left undeclared.
  `A` and `B` are arrow-only names here, the shape `recordField.ct`'s `/Sample` already had and the
  only shape the corpus had before its sibling. The program is otherwise the one next door, down to
  the two `data` lines it drops, so whether a source name ALSO has a data definition is the single
  variable between the two files — which is what makes a failure in one and not the other say what
  broke.
data(C)
data(Yes)

A= B

B= C

isC(c -> C) -> Yes
isC(c= C)= Yes

checkC= isC(c= C)

checkB= isC(c= B)

checkA= isC(c= A)
